stdnum4j
Copyright 2026 Jeferson Santos

This product includes software developed by Jeferson Santos.

The number validation rules are implemented from scratch against public
specifications. No code, data file or wording was taken from python-stdnum
(LGPL) or from any other implementation.

python-stdnum served as a behavioural reference only. Part of the test corpus
was imported from its test vectors and re-checked here; those fixtures live
under src/test/resources and are not part of any published artifact.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data files
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The library ships generated data files (*.dat) built from public registers.
Each file carries a header naming its own source; tools/README.md documents
how every one of them is produced. The sources that state a licence:

  stdnum4j-postal/src/main/resources/.../postal/postal-codes.dat
      Derived from Google's address metadata (libaddressinput),
      https://chromium-i18n.appspot.com/ssl-address/data/
      Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
      License (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

  stdnum4j-apac/src/main/resources/.../apac/cn-loc.dat
  stdnum4j-eu/src/main/resources/.../eu/at-fa.dat
  stdnum4j-international/src/main/resources/.../international/iban.dat
  stdnum4j-international/src/main/resources/.../international/imsi.dat
      Derived from Wikipedia tables, which mirror the official registers of
      the Chinese National Bureau of Statistics, the Austrian Federal Ministry
      of Finance, the SWIFT IBAN Registry and the ITU respectively.
      Wikipedia content is licensed CC BY-SA 4.0,
      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

The remaining data files reproduce code lists published by their issuing
bodies -- Payments NZ, the Czech National Bank, the National Bank of Belgium,
RTR Austria, Eurostat, GS1, SIX, the IEEE, the International ISBN Agency and
Badan Pusat Statistik. They are reproduced as factual registers, with
attribution, in the file header of each.
